In a new video from Vogue posted Tuesday (May 5), LISA, her stylist and designer Robert Wun take viewers behind the scenes of how the girl group star&#8217;s trippy avant-garde look came to life. Filmed during LISA&#8217;s final fitting before the Met the next day, the clip shows how she strapped on a pair of white mannequin-like arms &#8212; made from a 3D scan of her body &#8212; like a backpack, after which the team tried out different pieces of jewelry on her fake fingers and wrists.

&#8220;I am nervous for tomorrow, because my extra arms are really heavy,&#8221; LISA says at one point. &#8220;He said it&#8217;s 1.8 kilo, but I don&#8217;t think so. I think it&#8217;s heavier than that &#8212; but I have to fight through it.&#8221;

The final touch was a sheer white veil held up by the additional arms, making for a striking, theatrical look LISA effortlessly modeled on the carpet at the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York City on Monday (May 4). But before the event, she told Vogue , &#8220;I don&#8217;t want to trip tomorrow!&#8221;

All four of the BLACKPINK ladies attended the 2026 event, although LISA and bandmates JISOO, JENNIE and ROSÉ chose to walk the carpet separately. It marked the White Lotus star&#8217;s second time attending the gala, the theme of which this year was &#8220;Costume Art&#8221; with a dress code of &#8220;Fashion Is Art.&#8221;

